  <section>
    <h2>The Problem with Standard PokeAPI Portfolio Projects</h2>
    <p>A Pokédex is one of the most common projects developers build when learning frontend engineering. Hundreds of junior portfolios feature the exact same pattern: fetch 151 entries from the public PokeAPI, render static cards in a React grid, and attach a debounced search input.</p>
    <p>While effective for understanding basic asynchronous HTTP calls and component state, standard Pokédex clones fail to impress technical recruiters and engineering managers for three critical reasons:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Zero architectural differentiation:</strong> Most rely on bloated client-side single-page application (SPA) bundles that deliver poor Core Web Vitals, empty initial HTML shells, and sluggish mobile performance.</li>
      <li><strong>Passive consumption:</strong> Visitors browse static, pre-packaged data without any opportunity for real interaction, personal customization, or collaborative community contribution.</li>
      <li><strong>No production systems integration:</strong> They demonstrate isolated UI components without integrating backend CI/CD pipelines, automated testing, or schema-driven data validation.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>SM'S DEX was built to invert this dynamic: treating the Pokédex theme not as a superficial skin, but as a robust platform demonstrating production-grade software engineering, strict accessibility compliance, and community participation.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>System Architecture: Astro Islands & Semantic Performance</h2>
    <p>Rather than shipping a heavy client-side JavaScript runtime, SM'S DEX is built on <a href="https://astro.build/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Astro</a> with zero default client runtime overhead. Every page renders to pure, semantic HTML and CSS during the static build step, guaranteeing instant Largest Contentful Paint (LCP) and zero layout shift across devices.</p>
    <div class="grid">
      <article class="card">
        <h3>Dual-View Responsive Engine</h3>
        <p>The site offers both an authentic game-inspired handheld device presentation and an instant readable document view. Visitors on smaller screens or using assistive technology get clean semantic markup without forced horizontal scrollbars or spatial disorientation.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="card">
        <h3>Design System Tokens</h3>
        <p>Color styling dynamically adapts across nine distinct Pokémon generations using strict CSS custom properties. Each Pokémon entry drives contextual primary and secondary accents without runtime CSS-in-JS computation.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>How to Build a Pokédex Portfolio with Web Audio</h2>
    <p>Building a retro-style Pokédex portfolio with authentic chiptune audio requires solving two fundamental problems: asset weight and mobile autoplay policy restrictions. Typical projects fetch pre-recorded MP3 or WAV audio clips that add hundreds of kilobytes of network transfer and suffer from network latency jitter.</p>
    <p>To eliminate audio payloads entirely (0 KB asset footprint), SM'S DEX synthesizes Game Boy-style 8-bit sounds on the fly using the browser's native <a href="https://www.w3.org/TR/webaudio/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Web Audio API</a>:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Custom Oscillator Nodes:</strong> Generates square and pulse wave tones configured with rapid pitch decays (frequency modulation) to mimic classic handheld hardware sound generators.</li>
      <li><strong>Noise Burst Synthesis:</strong> Uses a <code>createBuffer</code> white noise generator passed through a high-pass biquad filter to synthesize mechanical button clicks and lid latch sounds.</li>
      <li><strong>Zero Network Latency:</strong> Because sounds are calculated mathematically in local memory, playback is instant (0ms buffer wait) upon user interaction.</li>
      <li><strong>Strict No-Autoplay Compliance:</strong> Audio remains completely suspended until explicit user interaction, fully honoring browser security policies and user consent.</li>
      <li><strong>Motion and Sensory Respect:</strong> The system actively queries <code>prefers-reduced-motion</code> to disable flashing screen animations and visual shake effects.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>The Open Roster: Turning GitHub Issues into Production PRs</h2>
    <p>The standout feature of SM'S DEX is its public community roster. Anyone can become an entry on the site simply by submitting a formatted GitHub issue.</p>
    <p>The entire onboarding pipeline is fully automated without requiring a separate database or server runtime:</p>
    <ol>
      <li><strong>Prefilled Form Templates:</strong> Visitors click "Add Pokémon" to open a GitHub issue with structured form inputs for sprite choice, typing, stats, moves, and flavor text.</li>
      <li><strong>Automated CI Validation:</strong> A <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/actions" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub Actions CI workflow</a> intercepts new issue submissions and validates every parameter against strict <a href="https://json-schema.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">JSON Schema</a> definitions (preventing invalid types, malicious inputs, or stat overflow).</li>
      <li><strong>Automated Pull Request Creation:</strong> Once validated, the automation generates a clean Git branch and opens a Pull Request updating the site's data records.</li>
      <li><strong>Production Build & Deploy:</strong> Upon maintainer merge, GitHub Pages builds and redeploys the site with the new Pokémon entry live on the roster.</li>
    </ol>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Comparison: SM'S DEX vs Typical Developer Clones</h2>
    <div class="grid">
      <article class="card">
        <h3>Standard PokeAPI Clone</h3>
        <p class="meta">Generic Tutorial Pattern</p>
        <p>Heavy client-side React/Vue bundle. Static PokeAPI mirror. Unstyled mobile layouts. Audio absent or loud uncompressed MP3s. No automated testing or community contribution.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="card">
        <h3>SM'S DEX Architecture</h3>
        <p class="meta">Engineered Production System</p>
        <p>Zero-JS default Astro architecture. Automated GitHub CI/CD roster pipeline. Synthesized Web Audio engine. 425+ automated test suites. Strict accessibility and reduced-motion standards.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

